      },
      "text": "Cancún to Chichén Itzá and the Ik Kil cenote"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8803eb26c8c6c40955c30dc46a97eb81c1da9c505028a95efc968f441f6eb926",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-5d356bbaac960a07",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Today you will visit the archaeological site of Chichén Itzá, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.\n\nThis extensive complex on the Yucatán Peninsula was an important centre of Maya civilisation at different periods and later came under Toltec influence. Its architecture reflects both traditions. Many stone structures survive across the site, and some have been restored.\n\nThe Pyramid of Kukulcán is the most prominent landmark at Chichén Itzá.\n\nAfter the tour, you will have time to swim in Ik Kil, a karst cenote. Its cool water offers a chance to unwind after walking around the archaeological site."
    },
